VERDICT
   26b-04 is REVERSED by the reading. The sentence measures TRUE. Chat 139 probed the rule's WORDS and
   found nothing, and said in terms that a token probe is not a reading; read as a MECHANISM the rule fires
   15 times over constraints proper and 21 times more over the checks of the same class, in a Register whose
   own definition makes every one of its 1628 entries a correction. *several* is reached under both readings
   of the count word in every cell of both conventions, the smallest cell being 15. The work also applies the
   rule and finds it does NOT fire 5 times (390, 439, 462, 900, 1061), which is the discipline the sentence
   describes rather than a counter-example to it. 3 members of the pool the reading cannot decide are carried
   as an upper bound and never assigned.
   What survives as a finding is not the count but the citation: 26b-11. The one instance E.1.5 names is a
   refutation by counterexample, and F.3 prints the rule in two forms that do not have one extent.
   New this unit: 26b-08 (§784 as a section pointer), 26b-09 (Thm 11.1 cited, printed nowhere), 26b-10
   (a build handle in the Register), 26b-11 (the two forms of the rule, and the instance that fits only one).

